<title>AUSTRALIA: Govt feels no pressure from Westpac bid-Costello.</title>
<headline>Govt feels no pressure from Westpac bid-Costello.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Treasurer Peter Costello said on Thursday the government felt no pressure to produce a quick reponse to Westpac Banking Corp's A$1.435 billion bid for the Bank of Melbourne.</p>
<p>&quot;The government doesn't feel in the slightest pressured by this,&quot; Costello told reporters.</p>
<p>Westpac's agreed merger with Bank of Melbourne, announced earlier on Thursday, is subject to government approval.</p>
</text>
